# XXI. Freedom has been reconstructed but not derived

Utpaladeva’s strongest account does not move merely from:

[
\text{self-awareness}
\rightarrow
\text{omnipotence}.
]

The more serious route is:

[
\text{manifestation}
\rightarrow
\text{determination}
\rightarrow
\text{selection}
\rightarrow
\text{action}.
]

Ratié’s work on Utpaladeva’s discussions of action shows that consciousness is treated as dynamic rather than as a static substance and that self-apprehension is connected with a subtle form of action. Utpaladeva also distinguishes the essence of action from the temporal sequence characteristic of limited action. ([Academia][16])

The strongest reconstruction is:

## P1

Manifestation is determinate.

[
M(x).
]

## P2

Determinate manifestation establishes:

[
x\text{ rather than }y.
]

## P3

Establishing one articulation rather than another is minimally selective.

## P4

Selection is a form of power:

[
Śakti_D.
]

## Provisional conclusion

[
\boxed{
\text{manifestation is not inert presence;}
}
]

it possesses:

[
\boxed{
\text{a minimal articulating efficacy.}
}
]

This is stronger than the lamp argument.

But three transitions remain:

[
\text{determination}
\not\Rightarrow
\text{causal intervention},
]

[
\text{local efficacy}
\not\Rightarrow
\text{causal independence},
]

[
\text{causal independence}
\not\Rightarrow
\text{unrestricted world-production}.
]

Therefore:

[
\boxed{
\text{minimal articulating power}
\not\Rightarrow
\textit{svātantrya}_{\infty}.
}
]

The final freedom claim depends on a further metaphysics of why the totality of determinate reality is nothing but consciousness’s articulation.

That has not yet been demonstrated.

