\text{agency}.
]

If they dissociate, Pratyabhijñā must explain why they remain expressions of one power.

If they cannot be coherently separated, the naturalist must explain why the relevant physical mechanisms always form one intrinsic unity.

---

# Final checkpoint

The deepest remaining question is not:

[
\text{Is consciousness fundamental?}
]

Nor:

[
\text{Is there one consciousness or many?}
]

Nor even:

[
\text{What makes a process conscious?}
]

It is:

[
\boxed{
\textbf{What establishes the domains within which manifestation}
}
]

[
\boxed{
\textbf{is jointly present and outside which it is absent?}
}
]

The subject is no longer best treated as the container of experience.

It is provisionally reconstructed as:

[
\boxed{
\textbf{a dynamically maintained exclusion profile within manifestation.}
}
]

The naturalist must explain why physical organization realizes such a profile.

The Buddhist must explain why momentary or processual manifestation forms one profile.

The pluralist must explain why one substance generates co-presence among its states.

The cosmopsychist must explain how one cosmic field decomposes into profiles.

Pratyabhijñā must explain why universal self-manifestation possesses the intrinsic power to form genuinely private profiles without becoming divided into independent substances.

The two chapters now terminate in one reciprocal bind:

[
\boxed{
\begin{aligned}
&\textbf{How can non-manifest structure produce phenomenal exclusion?}\
&\textbf{How can unrestricted manifestation produce phenomenal exclusion?}
\end{aligned}
}
]

The first is the sharpened naturalist problem.

The second is the sharpened Śaiva problem.

The missing object of theory is:

[
\boxed{
\Lambda
=======

\textbf{the law of perspectival partition}.
}
]

Until (\Lambda) is supplied, no theory has explained why reality manifests:

[
\boxed{
\textbf{here, together, as this, for this centre—and not elsewhere.}
}
]

The key breakthrough is that **Chapter 2 is not ultimately “the universalization chapter.”** It is the chapter on phenomenal domain formation. Universal consciousness, plural selves, process streams and physicalist integration are competing models of the same missing law.

